{
 "bank": "0C",
 "sections": {
  "s0CD22D": {
   "name": "Cutscene scene steps and object motion",
   "summary": [
    "Helpers for the credits/cutscene engine (scene handlers dispatched by [$13C6] and [$1442]) (state in [$1440]-[$144D], actor objects in $0B05-$0B8C).",
    "$0CD22D queues a 13-byte stripe image (VRAM update) and patches two tile words in it.",
    "$0CD283 shakes the screen +/-1 pixel on layer 1 X every frame. $0CD295-$0CD317 are scene-step handlers: play a sound,",
    "set timers/objects, advance [$1442] and jump to a CCxxx handler. $0CD33A moves object X in Y by its speed (1/16 pixel",
    "units); $0CD368 does the same for X. $0CD373 clears the subpixel bytes of objects 0-2 (quirk: $0B34 cleared twice).",
    "Object arrays (index = object): Y speed $0B05, X speed $0B14, Y/X subpixel $0B23/$0B32, Y/X pos $0B41/$0B50, hi $0B5F/$0B6E."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD386": {
   "name": "Table: debris initial Y speeds"
  },
  "s0CD396": {
   "name": "Table: debris initial X speeds"
  },
  "s0CD3A6": {
   "name": "Spawn and move falling debris",
   "summary": [
    "$0CD3A6: every other frame while 1 <= [$1445] <= $E7, take a free slot (14 down to 4) and launch a piece of debris",
    "near Mario (+$18,+$20) with speeds from the two tables and gravity 4. $0CD3F4: apply gravity (up to speed $40),",
    "move each active piece, free it when Y >= $80. Falls through into the draw routine at $0CD425."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD423": {
   "name": "Table: debris tiles"
  },
  "s0CD425": {
   "name": "Draw falling debris",
   "summary": [
    "Draws every active debris slot (14 down to 4) as an 8x8 sprite, tile alternating $3C/$3D, skipping X < $50."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD464": {
   "name": "Table: spark sprite Y offsets"
  },
  "s0CD484": {
   "name": "Table: spark sprite X offsets"
  },
  "s0CD4A4": {
   "name": "Draw sparks around Mario (JSL)",
   "summary": [
    "Called with JSL from bank 00 ($00C773). Draws up to three 8x8 sprites (tile $B6, prop $31) at offsets from Mario given",
    "by DATA_0CD484/0CD464 row [$1445]; offset $80 = skip. Y gets +8 when Mario is small."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD4F4": {
   "name": "Table: rising sprite tiles"
  },
  "s0CD4F8": {
   "name": "Rising and sideways sprites near Mario",
   "summary": [
    "$0CD4F8: when [$1446] is set, object 2 rises at speed -3 until $0D pixels above Mario and is drawn with tiles from",
    "DATA_0CD4F4 (prop $33). $0CD557: object 3 moves right/down from Mario and is drawn the same way; at X >= $0D it ends,",
    "clears [$1446] and advances [$1442]. $0CD5C6: advance the step, set [$1443] = $FF, [$144D] = $D0 and start",
    "sound/music value $13 through the STA.W $1DFB stored as data at $0CD5D5."
   ]
  },
  "Instr0CD5D5": {
   "name": "Start music $13 (code stored as data)",
   "summary": [
    "STA.W $1DFB written as .db bytes because the Mario-frame table at $0CD5D6 overlaps it; part of the routine above."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD5D9": {
   "name": "Table: Mario frame per animation tick"
  },
  "s0CD5E9": {
   "name": "Table: accessory tile and slot group"
  },
  "s0CD5FC": {
   "name": "Table: accessory OAM properties"
  },
  "s0CD60F": {
   "name": "Table: accessory X offsets"
  },
  "s0CD635": {
   "name": "Table: accessory Y offsets"
  },
  "s0CD65B": {
   "name": "Draw Mario accessory sprite (probably cape)",
   "summary": [
    "Runs when [$144A] >> 1 is non-zero. Plays a 16-tick animation counted down in [$1445] (sets Mario frame from",
    "the table at $0CD5D6), then draws one 16x16 sprite at $02FC (or $032C) relative to Mario, flipped with his facing.",
    "The tile, properties and offsets come from the tables at $0CD5E9-$0CD655, indexed by pose [$13DB] or tick."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD6C4": {
   "name": "Tables: three-tile sprite and column steps"
  },
  "s0CD6EC": {
   "name": "Draw three-tile sprite and move rope column",
   "summary": [
    "Runs when [$144A] >> 1 is non-zero. With [$1446] = 0 it draws three 16x16 sprites (tiles $8E,$8E,$8C) diagonally",
    "behind Mario (flipped with his direction). Otherwise it draws a column of five 16x16 sprites (tile $AC then $AE) at Mario X",
    "from Y = [$1446] - 1 (capped at $68), sets Mario frame $25/$38 and steps through [$1445]: move the column between Y $34",
    "and $68 in steps of 4, pausing [$1449] = $10 frames, with Mario walking right to the X targets. Purpose is a guess."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD7EB": {
   "name": "Tables: carried item position"
  },
  "s0CD803": {
   "name": "Carried item sprite and Mario exit walk",
   "summary": [
    "Called every frame from the cutscene update ($0CC98C). Draws a 16x16 sprite (tile 0, prop $21) following Mario at",
    "X = Mario - 9/10, with Y bobbing over 16 frames from DATA_0CD7F3. When Mario is still at X < $40 it starts the pick-up",
    "image timer ([$1498] = $10); when he reaches X <= 5 and is not moving left it increments [$144A] (scene done)."
   ]
  },
  "s0CD86F": {
   "name": "Padding: $FF fill"
  },
  "s0CD900": {
   "name": "Level layer 2 tilemap 1 (RLE)",
   "summary": [
    "RLE tilemap of 864 tiles for a level Layer 2 background, pointed to by Layer2Ptrs in bank 05 ($05E600).",
    "Token: bit 7 set = repeat next byte (count&$7F)+1 times; bit 7 clear = (count+1) literal bytes follow. Ends with $FF,$FF."
   ]
  },
  "s0CDAB9": {
   "name": "Level layer 2 tilemap 2 (RLE)",
   "summary": [
